  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "**CVE Numbering Authorities (CNAs).**\n\nThe CVE Program states that CVE Records are authored and published by CNAs (partners authorized to assign CVE IDs and publish records within a defined scope). Those published records make up the official CVE List.\n\nThe CVE Program also states that the CVE List feeds the NVD (NIST’s National Vulnerability Database). NVD then enriches those records (for example with reference tags, CVSS, CWE, and CPE). NVD’s own data model uses `sourceIdentifier` for the CNA that assigned the CVE.\n\nRelated points from CVE Program materials:\n- CVE and NVD are separate programs; the CVE List was started by MITRE in 1999 and NVD by NIST in 2005.\n- MITRE (via the HSSEDI FFRDC, sponsored by CISA) operates the CVE Program Secretariat and acts as a CNA of Last Resort, but individual records are attributed to the responsible CNA.\n- Optional extra data can also come from the CVE Program container or Authorized Data Publishers (ADPs); the core published CVE Record still comes from the CNA.\n\nSources: [cve.org related efforts / NVD](https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts), [cve.org FAQs](https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs), [cve.org process and glossary](https://www.cve.org/About/Process), [cve.org history](https://www.cve.org/about/history), [NVD CVE process/FAQs](https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process).",
